From: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:32:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rc: Fix build failure with CONFIG_LIRC disabled
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.61
Git-commit: 0c795849fd70d6bdb99aea5dd08d9b43128612f6

commit 0c795849fd70d6bdb99aea5dd08d9b43128612f6 upstream.

commit 37efd09ba2c6 ("media: rc: Ensure registered is cleared in error
path") broke the build if CONFIG_LIRC was not enabled.

Fixes: 37efd09ba2c6 ("media: rc: Ensure registered is cleared in error path")
Reported-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/oe-kbuild-all/202609230511.Em5Osw74-lkp@intel.com
Signed-off-by: Sean Young <sean@mess.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 drivers/media/rc/lirc_dev.c | 3 +++
 drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c  | 3 +--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/rc/lirc_dev.c b/drivers/media/rc/lirc_dev.c
index 7d4942925993..92f788683b5a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/rc/lirc_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/lirc_dev.c
@@ -775,6 +775,9 @@ void lirc_unregister(struct rc_dev *dev)
 	unsigned long flags;
 	struct lirc_fh *fh;
 
+	if (!device_is_registered(&dev->lirc_dev))
+		return;
+
 	dev_dbg(&dev->dev, "lirc_dev: driver %s unregistered from minor = %d\n",
 		dev->driver_name, MINOR(dev->lirc_dev.devt));
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c b/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
index cb1a087ed869..2f1684a81eb1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
+++ b/drivers/media/rc/rc-main.c
@@ -1981,8 +1981,7 @@ int rc_register_device(struct rc_dev *dev)
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &dev->lock)
 		dev->registered = false;
 
-	if (device_is_registered(&dev->lirc_dev))
-		lirc_unregister(dev);
+	lirc_unregister(dev);
 	device_del(&dev->dev);
 	/* registered already cleared above */
 	goto out_free_table;
-- 
2.56.0

